&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Content Creator - Content Creation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior AI Content Creator in the HelloFresh Studio, you are part of the AI Content Creation team and play a leading role in developing and scaling AI-powered content creation across mainly photography, but also supporting video, design, and emerging creative formats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You combine a strong background in commercial visual production with hands-on expertise in generative AI. You have a refined visual eye and strong creative judgment, allowing you to create high-quality content yourself and recognize what makes an image or video successful. Beyond creating individual assets, a key part of your role is translating creative direction and successful approaches into reliable, production-ready workflows that expand the Studio&#39;s AI capabilities. Working closely with art directors, photographers, retouchers, video, design, and tech, you identify where AI can improve creative possibilities, production efficiency, and scale. You help define best practices, evaluate emerging technologies, and continuously develop how AI is used in visual production across the Studio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high-quality AI-powered content across commercial photography and video, including lifestyle, food, product, and campaign content, translating creative direction into assets ready for real production and marketing use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine AI content creation workflows, prompts, techniques, and reusable approaches using tools such as Krea, Higgsfield, Claude, ComfyUI, and emerging platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Art Directors, Photographers, Video, Design, and Post-Production to translate creative concepts and established visual approaches into scalable AI-powered production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your creative judgment and production experience to continuously improve visual quality, realism, consistency, and efficiency across AI-generated content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Workflow Specialists to identify automation opportunities and help turn successful creative processes into scalable or automated content-generation workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging AI models, tools, and techniques, testing their practical value and introducing those that meaningfully improve creative output or production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and share best practices, standards, and documentation for AI content creation, and support colleagues in developing their AI capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay closely connected to developments in generative AI, actively experimenting with new approaches and identifying opportunities to expand what the Studio can create.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of professional experience in commercial photography, retouching, art direction, or a closely related visual production discipline&lt;/strong&gt;, with a strong understanding of professional photography and/or video production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced hands-on experience creating high-quality visual content with generative AI tools and integrating AI into real creative or production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A refined visual eye and strong creative judgment&lt;/strong&gt;, with an excellent understanding of photography, composition, lighting, colour, visual storytelling, realism, and what makes commercial imagery feel premium and intentional.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to interpret creative briefs and translate creative direction into high-quality visual content and repeatable production approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across creative, production, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proactive, curious, and solution-oriented, with a strong sense of ownership, an experimental mindset, and genuine enthusiasm for emerging AI technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please include a portfolio of your recent and relevant work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; is a leading AI-powered performance marketing platform for the mobile app economy. Our end-to-end technology stack helps app marketers acquire and retain high-value users, while enabling publishers to maximize revenue across programmatic and direct demand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff’s solutions, including Accelerate, Direct, Monetize, Intelligence, and Vungle Exchange, support over 6,600 mobile businesses across 74 countries in sectors such as gaming, social, finance, ecommerce, and entertainment. Founded in 2012 and headquartered in Redwood City, CA, Liftoff has a diverse, global presence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is looking for a Commercial Legal Counsel that will assist the in-house legal department with Insertion Orders (Agreements), third party contracts and other legal needs. This position will support the Commercial, Finance and Accounting teams, located around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Commercial Legal Counsel at Liftoff, you will play a pivotal role in ensuring the seamless execution of contracts that drive our business forward. You will be at the intersection of legal expertise, meticulous organization, and collaborative teamwork. Your responsibilities will encompass contract drafting, negotiation, process improvement and training. As an essential part of our team, you&#39;ll contribute to the foundation of our business relationships and help us navigate the complex world of contracts with precision and efficiency. If you&#39;re passionate about detail-oriented work, contract law, and making a meaningful impact, this role is your opportunity to shine. Join us in shaping the way we manage contracts and elevate our commitment to excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and negotiate a wide range of contracts, including vendor agreements, customer contracts, and licensing agreements, to ensure compliance with company policies and legal requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal teams, including legal, sales/commercial, product, engineering, finance and accounting to understand contract terms, resolve issues, and provide guidance on contractual matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an organized and up-to-date contract ticketing system, respond to each contract ticket in a timely manner and track contract milestones and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in&amp;nbsp; contract compliance, addressing any deviations or breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and improvement of contract templates and standard clauses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the contract approval process, ensuring proper authorization and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance and training to employees on contract-related matters and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on relevant laws and regulations impacting contract management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-8 years&#39; PQE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Law, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Contracts Counsel/Legal Counsel or in a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of contract law and legal terminology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with exceptional organizational and time management abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in contract management software or tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in a cross-functional team environment globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in ad-tech is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in London or remotely within the United Kingdom, occasionally going into the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a contract position with the potential to become a full-time employee. The expected hours of work required for this position are 35 to 40 hours per week, with occasional early evening hours for team meetings, as the manager is located in our Redwood City office in California.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
